{"institution":{"city":"Alfred","kind":"private","name":"Alfred University","state":"NY"},"plan":{"allow_repeated_courses":true,"catalog_year":"2024-2025","degree":"BS","id":"alfred-university-bs-electrical-engineering","major":"Electrical Engineering","notes":"Source: Alfred University Inamori School of Engineering official 'Suggested Curriculum Course Plan' (SCCP) for Electrical Engineering, 'for students entering Fall 2024 - Spring 2025', edited June 7, 2024 (my.alfred.edu/engineering/_docs/eegr-2024-25.pdf). This is the newest term-by-term plan the school publishes; the 2026-2027 AU Catalog (undergraduatecatalog.alfred.edu) publishes requirement lists only. Semester credit sums transcribed exactly as published: 16+17+16+18+15+19+16+15 = 132, matching the published Total Credits: 132 (engineering bachelor's: 126-130 typical; EE plans run slightly higher; SOE minimum requirement 128). Prerequisite ordering verified: MATH 151->152->253->271; CHEM 105->106; PHYS 125->126; ENGR 220 (Circuit Theory I, Sem 4) before ELEC 321 (Circuit Theory II, Sem 5); ELEC 210 Digital Logic (Sem 3) before ELEC 310 Microprocessor Systems (Sem 6). 0-credit labs (CHEM 105L etc. are 1 cr; ENGR 117L, PHYS 125L/126L, ELEC 210L/220L/321L/356L, ENGR 160/360 are 0 cr) are official recurring seminar/lab slots transcribed with required_zero:true. ENGR 160 (Sem 1-2), ENGR 360 (Sem 3-8), and ENGR 490 capstone (Sem 7-8, 2+2 with the same instructor per the published capstone rule) repeat by official design - allow_repeated_courses:true. Semester 4 computing slot is an official either/or: CSCI 156 Computer Science I OR RNEW 303 Software Engineering (transcribed as a choice). EE Elective (6 cr): one published sequence - Computer Engineering (VLSI Design / Computer Architecture), Renewable Energy (RNEW 432 Solar Energy / RNEW 431 Wind Energy), Controls (ELEC 422 / ELEC 423), or Power Engineering (ELEC 433 Modern Electric Grids / ELEC 441 Advanced Power Electronics). Technical Electives (6 cr): most 300/400-level CEMS, CHEM, ELEC, ENGR, MATH, MECH, PHYS, RNEW (except CHEM 343, MATH 331, MECH 320, unapproved Topics); or FIN 348 / MGMT 328; or COOP 385 / ENGR 385 internship. ENGL 101 'if required otherwise General Education elective (2-4)'. AU degree rules per plan: Global Perspective, Wellness/PE, 2.0 GPA with no more than 7 credits of D/D+ in engineering courses, 60-credit SOE General Education. Verify: Alfred State College (SUNY tech college in the same town) is a DIFFERENT school and was separately blocked/collected; this plan is Alfred University (private).","semesters":[{"courses":[{"category":"core","choice":false,"choice_note":"'ENGL 101 if required otherwise General Education elective (2-4)'.","code":"ENGL 101","credits":4,"options":[],"prereq":[],"title":"Writing I"},{"category":"core","choice":false,"choice_note":"","code":"MATH 151","credits":4,"options":[],"prereq":[],"title":"Calculus I"},{"category":"core","choice":false,"choice_note":"","code":"CHEM 105","credits":3,"options":[],"prereq":[],"title":"General Chemistry I"},{"category":"core","choice":false,"choice_note":"","code":"CHEM 105L","credits":1,"options":[],"prereq":[],"title":"General Chemistry I Laboratory"},{"category":"core","choice":false,"choice_note":"","code":"ENGR 101","credits":2,"options":[],"prereq":[],"title":"Introduction to Engineering"},{"category":"core","choice":false,"choice_note":"","code":"ENGR 117","credits":2,"options":[],"prereq":[],"title":"Engineering Foundations II & Lab"},{"category":"core","choice":false,"choice_note":"","code":"ENGR 117L","credits":0,"options":[],"prereq":[],"required_zero":true,"title":"Engineering Foundations II Lab"},{"category":"core","choice":false,"choice_note":"","code":"ENGR 160","credits":0,"options":[],"prereq":[],"required_zero":true,"title":"First-Year Seminar"}],"declared_credits":16,"label":"Semester 1","n":1},{"courses":[{"category":"core","choice":false,"choice_note":"","code":"MATH 152","credits":4,"options":[],"prereq":["MATH 15